// expect: refuse E_PatternInexhaustive
// THE EXHAUSTIVENESS CHECK READS THE WHOLE PATTERN (2026-10-13): a variant
// missing INSIDE a constructor's payload is a value the match does not cover,
// and the refusal names it — `Wrap(Three)` here. Until this landed the check
// read each arm's top constructor alone: `Wrap(One)` and `Wrap(Two)` named
// `Wrap`, the only top beside `Bare`, so the match passed, and the program
// trapped when `Three` arrived — measured 2026-10-13 on boot ad930774, where
// this program compiled clean and exited 134 at the arm nobody wrote. The
// compiler's own classifier walk did the same the day a statement variant was
// added, which is how the gap was found.
type Inner = One | Two | Three

type Outer = Wrap(Inner) | Bare

fn pick(o) = match o {
  Wrap(One) => 1,
  Wrap(Two) => 2,
  Bare => 0,
}

fn main() = pick(Wrap(Three))
